  "detail": "Thank you: review confirmed the guard rejects every compound form at the top level. It confirmed this repository's check and `retry_files` stay eligible, and that the non-targeted retries are unchanged.\n\n`singleBunTest(cfg.retryFiles)` checks the template before the filenames are substituted (~src/gates/run.ts:336). `quoteRetryFiles` quotes for an unquoted shell context, so a template such as `bun test \"{files}\"` passes the check. A failing test file named `test/x\"; true #.test.ts` then expands to `bun test \"'./test/x\"; true #.test.ts'\"`, whose exit status comes from `true`. Review reproduced this with real Bun: the original failure had complete attribution, and the targeted retry returned `ok: true` without re-running the failing test.\n\nFix:\n- Accept `retry_files` only when `{files}` appears exactly once as a standalone, unquoted shell word.\n- Also run `singleBunTest` on the expanded command before executing it on the targeted-only path; refuse with a skip reason if it fails.\n\nAdd this test from review (adjust helpers to fit), make it pass and don't weaken it:\n\n```ts\ntest(\"a quoted retry placeholder cannot turn a failing test into a shell success\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture();\n  try {\n    const file = 'test/x\"; true #.test.ts';\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(f.cwd, file),\n      'import { test, expect } from \"bun:test\"; test(\"still fails\", () => expect(1).toBe(2));',\n    );\n    const check = {\n      ...testCheck,\n      run: 'bun test --reporter=junit --reporter-outfile=\"$LIMITLESS_GATE_REPORT\"',\n    };\n    const cfg = { ...config, checks: [check], retryFiles: 'bun test \"{files}\"' };\n    await confinementScope.run(fakeConfinement, async () => {\n      const run = await runLocalGates(f.cwd, cfg, signal, { env: bunEnv });\n      const original = run.checks[0];\n      if (!original) throw new Error(\"Missing original check\");\n      expect(original.ok).toBe(false);\n      expect(original.failureAttributionComplete).toBe(true);\n      expect(original.failedFiles).toEqual([file]);\n      const retries = await retryFailures(\n        [{ check, original }],\n        f.cwd,\n        cfg,\n        signal,\n        undefined,\n        (retry) => runLocalGates(f.cwd, retry, signal, { env: bunEnv }),\n        true,\n      );\n      expect(retries.get(original)?.ok ?? false).toBe(false);\n    });\n  } finally {\n    f.close();\n  }\n});\n\n```"
